  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have $a=\\sqrt{9}=3$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$",
